# What boot starts once the drivers are running: from the system volume,
# when / is one, or from the initramfs. A shell on the serial line, the
# first, which boot waits for, so that its exit stops the system; its
# terminal is console, which uart serves. wm, the compositor, owns the
# screen through display and keeps windows on it for its clients; the
# two vts are terminals in two of them, named vt1 and vt2 in the order
# they start, each starting its own shell, sh vt1 and sh vt2, and closing
# when it exits.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/wm
start /Applications/Terminal.app/vt
start /Applications/Terminal.app/vt
